TASK 6 – Read and Print Data Correctly (4 Marks)
1. Brief explanation
In C, scanf() reads input and printf() displays output. The format specifier must match the variable's data type. Using the wrong specifier can cause incorrect output or undefined behavior.
Data type	scanf() specifier	printf() specifier
int	%d	%d
unsigned int	%u	%u
long	%ld	%ld
long long	%lld	%lld
float	%f	%f
double	%lf	%f
char	%c	%c
Character string	%s	%s

Important: For scanf(), use %f for float and %lf for double. For printf(), %f is used to print both float values (promoted to double) and double values.

To detect invalid input, check the return value of scanf(). For example, scanf("%d", &units) != 1 indicates that a valid integer was not read.

CODE:


#include <stdio.h>

#define SLAB1_UNITS 100
#define SLAB2_UNITS 200
#define RATE2_PAISE 225LL
#define RATE3_PAISE 450LL
#define FIXED_CHARGE_PAISE 5000LL

int main(void)
{
    int household, units;
    char category;
    long long energy = 0;
    long long total;

    printf("Enter household number, category and units: ");

    if (scanf("%d %c %d", &household, &category, &units) != 3)
    {
        printf("Invalid input! Enter valid values.\n");
        return 1;
    }

    if (household <= 0 || units < 0)
    {
        printf("Invalid household number or units.\n");
        return 1;
    }

    if (units > SLAB1_UNITS)
    {
        int slab2 = (units < SLAB2_UNITS)
                        ? units - SLAB1_UNITS
                        : SLAB2_UNITS - SLAB1_UNITS;

        energy += (long long)slab2 * RATE2_PAISE;
    }

    if (units > SLAB2_UNITS)
    {
        energy += (long long)(units - SLAB2_UNITS)
                  * RATE3_PAISE;
    }

    total = energy + FIXED_CHARGE_PAISE;

    printf("\n--- Electricity Bill ---\n");
    printf("Household number: %d\n", household);
    printf("Category: %c\n", category);
    printf("Units consumed: %d\n", units);

    printf("Energy charge: Rs. %lld.%02lld\n",
           energy / 100, energy % 100);

    printf("Fixed charge: Rs. %lld.%02lld\n",
           FIXED_CHARGE_PAISE / 100,
           FIXED_CHARGE_PAISE % 100);

    printf("Total bill: Rs. %lld.%02lld\n",
           total / 100, total % 100);

    return 0;
}

SAMPLE INPUT:
1001 D 150

OUTPUT:

Enter household number, category and units: 1001 D 150

--- Electricity Bill ---
Household number: 1001
Category: D
Units consumed: 150
Energy charge: Rs. 112.50
Fixed charge: Rs. 50.00
Total bill: Rs. 162.50




